From 8caa32a10f79aa5e35e008054b29a233e59d8fde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:01:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Cost estimate: weight prices by consumption, label it as
 an estimate

- The estimate priced all consumption at ONE plain average of the month's
  prices. Heat pump and rest of the house now use prices weighted by the hours
  they were used in: sum(kWh*price)/sum(kWh) over hours with both
- New api.php?action=hourly-consumption (HourlyConsumption: hourly deltas of the
  cumulative meters with the same reset rule as lagDelta, gaps spread evenly,
  EV home charging spread over the hours it ran, rest = house - hp - ev)
- pricing.js (pure, node-tested); elvarmeCost takes optional per-component
  rates and equals the old model when they are equal (20k random checks)
- Falls back to the plain average if hourly consumption is unavailable
- 'Forventet elregning' says: estimate, excl. subscription; tooltip explains
  the basis
- Remove stray routes/DatabaseManager.php
